    {
      "parameters": {
        "text": "={{ \"MIND DUMP:\\n\" + ($json.brain_dump || \"\")  }}",
        "schemaType": "manual",
        "inputSchema": "{\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"capacity_signal\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"enum\": [\"low\", \"normal\", \"high\", \"unknown\"]\n    },\n    \"capacity_evidence\": {\n      \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"]\n    },\n    \"available_minutes\": {\n      \"type\": [\"number\", \"null\"]\n    },\n    \"items\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"source_text\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"description\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"item_type\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"enum\": [\"task\", \"event\", \"idea\", \"reference\", \"concern\"]\n          },\n          \"status\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"enum\": [\"open\", \"completed\", \"scheduled\", \"informational\"]\n          },\n          \"deadline_text\": {\n            \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"]\n          },\n          \"effort_band\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"enum\": [\"quick\", \"low\", \"medium\", \"high\", \"unknown\"]\n          },\n          \"needs_clarification\": {\n            \"type\": \"boolean\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\n          \"source_text\",\n          \"description\",\n          \"item_type\",\n          \"status\",\n          \"deadline_text\",\n          \"effort_band\",\n          \"needs_clarification\"\n        ],\n        \"additionalProperties\": false\n      }\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"capacity_signal\",\n    \"capacity_evidence\",\n    \"available_minutes\",\n    \"items\"\n  ],\n  \"additionalProperties\": false\n}",
        "options": {
          "systemPromptTemplate": "You extract structured information for LoopLight.\n\nSeparate temporary capacity information from persistent items.\n\nCapacity rules:\n- Infer capacity_signal only from what the user says about their current energy or ability.\n- Use unknown when capacity is not provided.\n- Extract available_minutes only when the user gives or clearly implies an amount of time.\n- Never carry capacity from an earlier submission.\n\nItem rules:\n- Preserve each item's original wording in source_text.\n- Create one item for each distinct task, event, idea, reference, or concern.\n- Do not invent a deadline.\n- Mark something completed only when the user explicitly says it is already done.\n- Use scheduled for an event with a stated date or time.\n- Use informational for ideas or references that do not require action.\n\nEffort rules:\n- quick: under 30 minutes\n- low: 30 to 60 minutes\n- medium: over 60 to 120 minutes\n- high: over 120 minutes\n- unknown: not enough information\n- Effort is an estimate, not a confirmed fact.\n\nFor effort_band, classify based on the nature of the task itself, inferring when not explicit:\n- quick: a single action taking a few minutes , under 30 (a reply, a quick call, checking something)\n- low: a short focused task under 60 min (a short email, a small errand)\n- medium: a task needing 60-120 min of real focus (drafting something, a longer errand, prep work)\n- high: a task needing 120+ min or spanning multiple sessions (a project, something complex/unclear in scope)\n\nOnly use \"unknown\" if there's genuinely no way to infer effort from the text — this should be rare, not the default. Make your best reasonable guess based on the task's nature before falling back to unknown.\n\nClarification rules:\n- Set needs_clarification to true only when ambiguity would prevent the item from being understood or acted upon.\n- Do not request clarification merely because effort or deadline is unknown.\n-If the brain dump is empty, just says \"nothing,\" or is clearly not describing any real task/thought (e.g. \"n/a\", \"just checking in\"), return an empty items array — don't invent a task from filler text."
        }
      },
